WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.985
See the evidence before the answer.

2
00:00:02.265 --> 00:00:05.781
This independent prototype opens on an
analytical index.

3
00:00:06.061 --> 00:00:08.583
It packages eighty digest-bound records.

4
00:00:08.863 --> 00:00:13.078
They cover GOV.UK content, public data and
APIs.

5
00:00:13.358 --> 00:00:16.954
The worked answer identifies three
official starting points.

6
00:00:17.234 --> 00:00:19.914
They cover what to check after a baby is
born.

7
00:00:20.194 --> 00:00:24.214
Observation times, scope and the main
limitation stay visible.

8
00:00:24.500 --> 00:00:28.213
The Evidence Trace visualises the same
deterministic material.

9
00:00:28.493 --> 00:00:32.798
Follow a labelled path from answer to
claim, source and transformation.

10
00:00:33.078 --> 00:00:37.072
Then inspect its packaged SHA-two-five-six
check and limitation.

11
00:00:37.352 --> 00:00:41.627
Every relationship is text-labelled;
colour never carries meaning alone.

12
00:00:41.908 --> 00:00:45.369
Select one foundation to inspect authority
and assertion.

13
00:00:45.649 --> 00:00:48.171
Verification and freshness stay separate.

14
00:00:48.451 --> 00:00:52.727
Integrity, access, rights and coverage
stay separate too.

15
00:00:53.007 --> 00:00:55.227
Nothing is collapsed into a trust score.

16
00:00:55.507 --> 00:00:58.500
The authoritative page and limitations
remain visible.

17
00:00:58.781 --> 00:01:01.000
Compare two claims field by field.

18
00:01:01.280 --> 00:01:05.357
Each keeps its official source,
observation time and limitation.

19
00:01:05.637 --> 00:01:08.920
The table declares no winner and makes no
personal decision.

20
00:01:09.214 --> 00:01:13.571
A supported Codex in-app browser receipt
records five native page tools.

21
00:01:13.851 --> 00:01:17.858
Three inspect verified data; two
reversibly update the page.

22
00:01:18.138 --> 00:01:21.276
All five were called against this exact
public release.

23
00:01:21.556 --> 00:01:25.257
The comparison used the same answer and
claims as the human view.

24
00:01:25.537 --> 00:01:28.477
Its canonical and displayed result digests
match.

25
00:01:28.757 --> 00:01:33.079
No provider, storage, catalogue or
external state changed.

26
00:01:33.359 --> 00:01:38.540
A manual Safari VoiceOver journey uses the
same public release without WebMCP.

27
00:01:38.820 --> 00:01:42.515
It covers headings, controls and selected
foundations.

28
00:01:42.795 --> 00:01:46.700
It also covers comparison, live status and
source links.

29
00:01:46.980 --> 00:01:49.084
Results and limitations are recorded.

30
00:01:49.364 --> 00:01:53.588
This is not a Web Content Accessibility
Guidelines conformance claim.

31
00:01:53.868 --> 00:01:58.289
Final frames show the link’s accessible
name and restored comparison focus.

32
00:01:58.568 --> 00:02:01.050
The evidence estate makes scope explicit.

33
00:02:01.330 --> 00:02:04.846
Two reviewed collections supply all eighty
searchable records.

34
00:02:05.126 --> 00:02:07.452
Eight others are described but not
searchable.

35
00:02:07.732 --> 00:02:11.171
A descriptor never admits a producer
payload by itself.

36
00:02:11.451 --> 00:02:15.414
Every result keeps an authoritative human
link and limitations visible.

37
00:02:15.694 --> 00:02:19.314
This is an independent prototype, not an
official service.

38
00:02:19.594 --> 00:02:22.546
It grants no access and is not a durable
gateway.
